course: dictionary
lesson: 5064
title: Inspire and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inspire means to give someone the wish and the energy to do something good or creative. «Her talk inspired us to recycle.» The talk made the children want to recycle, so inspired means something gave them the push to act.
explain: Inspire can also mean that something gave someone an idea. «The Amazon giant water lily has ribs underneath that inspired the Crystal Palace in London.» The ribs gave the builders an idea for their design. When you see inspired by, ask: what gave the idea?
explain: Inspire can also mean to make people feel a feeling, as in «inspire confidence» or «inspire fear». Swap in a meaning to check it: «make people feel confident» fits, so you know it is right.
fact: Inspire means to give someone the wish and energy to do something good or creative.
fact: «Inspired by» means something gave someone the idea for their work.
fact: «Inspire» can also mean to make people feel a feeling, as in «inspire fear».
fact: «Praying Mantis» style is said to have been «inspired by» watching a mantis fight.
fact: In science, inspire is a rare word meaning to breathe in.
exercise: «Her talk inspired us to recycle.» What does inspired mean here? | Taught us to swim | *Gave us the wish and energy to do something good | Made us fall asleep | Made us very hungry
exercise: Toad Hall is said to have been «inspired by» big houses on the Thames. What does inspired by mean? | Was painted on a wall | Was built next to a river | *Had the idea for it come from them | Was bought from a shop
exercise: «The ribs of the lily inspired the Crystal Palace.» Find and copy the word that shows the ribs gave the builders an idea. | London | ribs | Crystal | *inspired
test: «The coach's words inspired the team to fight back.» What does inspired mean here? | Made the team go home | Made the team very tired | *Gave the team the wish and energy to try hard | Taught the team to cook
test: «Stories of brave heroes inspire others.» What does inspire mean here? | To fall asleep | To hide from danger | To breathe out slowly | *To give people the wish and energy to do good things
exam: What does «inspire confidence» mean? | To breathe out slowly | *To make people feel confident | To buy a new coat | To lose your confidence
